{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"undamaged-adept-xenarthra","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/llm/runner.py` (the two `record()` call sites around the structured and agentic run paths) reads `req.target.get(\"ticket_id\")` when building the usage-log row, but every producer of `target` writes the plural key `ticket_ids` (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/runs.py` and `src/rebar/llm/operations.py`). Result: 0 of the ~11,900 rows in `.rebar/usage.jsonl` carry a ticket, so per-ticket (and therefore per-review) cost attribution from the usage log is impossible, and `docs/llm-framework.md`'s claim that rows carry `ticket` is false. The eval ledger needs per-run attribution and this is the cheapest fix on that path.\n\n## Approach\n\nRead `ticket_ids` (first element, or the joined list) at both call sites, keep accepting the singular key for compatibility, and correct the doc sentence. Do not change the producers' key.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner.py`\n- `docs/llm-framework.md`\n- `tests/unit/test_usage_log.py` (or the existing runner usage test)\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit: a request whose target carries `ticket_ids=[id]` yields a usage row with `ticket == id`; one carrying the legacy singular key still works; one with neither yields `ticket=None`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] New usage-log rows produced by a gate session carry the ticket id; checked by running one `review-plan` locally (or the Tier-1 commissioning run) and inspecting the rows.\n- [ ] The regression test above passes in `make test`.\n- [ ] `docs/llm-framework.md` describes the actual field.","id":"860f-8886-a17b-48f1","parent_id":"759e-7dc1-675c-4877","priority":2,"tags":["llm","usage-log","cost"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"usage_log rows never carry a ticket id: runner reads target[\"ticket_id\"] but producers write \"ticket_ids\""},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788029201914191916,"uuid":"9a761a83-0748-4b4f-9168-a5481b74ea64"}